    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Civic responsibilities</span> are the duties every citizen owes to the state and to fellow citizens, so that society can function peacefully and develop. The Bible teaches that Christians, as citizens of both heaven and earth, must take these duties seriously.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Civic Responsibilities</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Civic responsibilities are the obligations a citizen owes to their country and community, arising from being a member of that society and enjoying its benefits and protection.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Examples of Civic Responsibilities</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Obedience to the laws of the land.</li><li>Payment of taxes.</li><li>Voting and participating in elections.</li><li>Community service and voluntary work.</li><li>Protecting public property and the environment.</li><li>Respecting the rights of others.</li><li>Defending the nation when necessary.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Importance of Civic Responsibilities in Nation Building</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>They promote peace, order and security in society.</li><li>They provide government with revenue (through taxes) for development projects.</li><li>They strengthen democracy through active citizen participation.</li><li>They build a sense of national unity and belonging.</li><li>They reduce crime and social vices.</li><li>They ensure that public resources and amenities are protected and maintained.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Biblical Teaching on Civic Duties — Romans 13:1–7</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">In Romans 13:1–7, Paul teaches that every person should submit to governing authorities, since all authority is established by God, and those who resist it are resisting what God has instituted. Christians are to obey the law, pay taxes, and give honour and respect to whom they are due, not merely out of fear of punishment but for the sake of conscience.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Be ready to quote and explain Romans 13:1–7 as the key biblical passage supporting civic responsibility and submission to government.</div>",
