    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">HIV</span> (Human Immunodeficiency Virus) is a virus that attacks the body's immune system, while <span class=\"learn-keyword\">AIDS</span> (Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome) is the advanced stage of HIV infection, when the immune system is severely weakened.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of HIV and AIDS</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">HIV is the virus that causes infection; AIDS is the final, most severe stage of the disease it causes, where the body can no longer fight off infections and illnesses effectively.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Causes and Modes of Transmission</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Mode of transmission</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Unprotected sexual intercourse</td><td>With an infected person, the most common mode worldwide</td></tr><tr><td>Blood transfusion</td><td>With infected, unscreened blood</td></tr><tr><td>Sharing sharp objects</td><td>Needles, syringes, razor blades or other objects contaminated with infected blood</td></tr><tr><td>Mother-to-child transmission</td><td>During pregnancy, childbirth, or breastfeeding</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"learn-p\">HIV is <strong>not</strong> transmitted by casual contact such as hugging, shaking hands, sharing food, or mosquito bites.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Biblical Perspectives on Sexual Purity</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">The Bible consistently teaches sexual purity and faithfulness. 1 Corinthians 6:18–20 instructs believers to flee sexual immorality, since the body is a temple of the Holy Spirit. Hebrews 13:4 teaches that marriage should be honoured and the marriage bed kept pure. These teachings directly support behaviour that reduces the risk of HIV transmission.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Consequences of Immoral Living</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Increased risk of contracting HIV and other sexually transmitted infections.</li><li>Broken relationships, families and trust.</li><li>Guilt, shame and spiritual separation from God.</li><li>Social stigma and its effects on mental health.</li><li>Unwanted pregnancy and its related challenges.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Preventive Measures</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Abstinence from premarital sex and faithfulness within marriage.</li><li>Avoiding the sharing of sharp objects such as needles and razors.</li><li>Screening of blood before transfusion.</li><li>Use of sterile medical equipment.</li><li>Voluntary counselling and testing (VCT) to know one's status.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Distinguish clearly between how HIV IS transmitted and common myths about how it is NOT transmitted.</div>",
