    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">Beyond the biological facts of HIV/AIDS, Christians must also address the myths that fuel stigma, and respond to those affected with compassion rather than condemnation.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Myths and Misconceptions about HIV/AIDS</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Myth</th><th>Fact</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>HIV can be spread by hugging, shaking hands or sharing food/utensils</td><td>HIV is not spread by casual, everyday contact</td></tr><tr><td>Mosquito bites spread HIV</td><td>Mosquitoes do not transmit HIV</td></tr><tr><td>A person with HIV always looks visibly sick</td><td>A person can carry HIV for years without visible symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>HIV only affects certain groups of people</td><td>Anyone, regardless of age, gender or status, can contract HIV</td></tr><tr><td>AIDS is a death sentence with no way to manage it</td><td>With antiretroviral therapy (ART), people living with HIV can live long, productive lives</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Effects on Individuals, Families and Society</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Individuals: physical weakening, psychological trauma, and discrimination.</li><li>Families: loss of breadwinners, orphaned children, and financial strain from medical care.</li><li>Society: loss of a productive workforce, strain on healthcare systems, and the social cost of stigma.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Role of Christians in Showing Care and Compassion</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Christians are called to love their neighbours as themselves (Mark 12:31) and to care for the sick, as Jesus demonstrated throughout His ministry by touching and healing those others avoided, including lepers. Christians should support people living with HIV through acceptance, encouragement, practical help, and by combating stigma and discrimination within the church and community.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Biblical Support for Healthy Living</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">1 Corinthians 6:19–20 reminds believers that their bodies are temples of the Holy Spirit and should be honoured through healthy, disciplined living. 3 John 1:2 expresses the wish that believers may prosper and be in good health, affirming that physical wellbeing matters to God alongside spiritual health.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Summary:</strong> The Christian response to HIV/AIDS should combine biblical standards of purity with compassion, correct information, and active care for those affected.</div>",
