    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\">The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">dignity of labour</span> is the belief that all honest work, whatever its nature, deserves respect, and that work itself is valuable and worthy, not shameful.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Labour</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Labour refers to any physical or mental effort or work done, usually in exchange for payment or to accomplish a task, whether in farming, trading, teaching, cleaning or any other honest occupation.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Biblical View on Work</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Passage</th><th>Teaching</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Genesis 2:15</td><td>God placed Adam in the Garden of Eden to work it and take care of it — work existed even before the Fall, as part of God's original design for humanity</td></tr><tr><td>Proverbs 22:29</td><td>A skilled, diligent worker will stand before kings, not before obscure men — diligence in one's work leads to honour and advancement</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Importance of Dignity in Labour</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>It affirms that no honest job is beneath a person's worth.</li><li>It encourages excellence and diligence in whatever work one does.</li><li>It builds self-respect and the respect of others.</li><li>It contributes to personal and national economic development.</li><li>It reflects good stewardship of the abilities God has given.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Consequences of Idleness</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Poverty and lack (Proverbs 10:4, 'Lazy hands make for poverty').</li><li>Loss of self-respect and purpose.</li><li>Increased temptation toward dishonest means of survival, including crime.</li><li>Burden on family and society.</li><li>Wasted God-given talents and time.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Relevance of Honest Work in Contemporary Society</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">In today's society, where many seek quick, dishonest wealth, the Christian teaching on the dignity of labour calls believers to value patient, honest work over shortcuts, recognising that true and lasting success comes through diligence and integrity.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Summary:</strong> Work is not a curse but part of God's original plan for humanity; all honest labour deserves dignity and respect.</div>",
