    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Corruption</span> is the dishonest or unethical use of power, position or resources, especially for personal gain, at the expense of others and of society. The Bible strongly condemns corruption in all its forms.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Corruption</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Corruption is the abuse of entrusted power or position for private benefit, often involving dishonesty, deception or the betrayal of trust placed in an individual.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Forms of Corruption</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bribery</td><td>Offering or accepting money or favours to influence a decision or action unfairly</td></tr><tr><td>Fraud</td><td>Deliberate deception for financial or personal gain</td></tr><tr><td>Nepotism</td><td>Favouring relatives or friends unfairly, especially in appointments or opportunities</td></tr><tr><td>Dishonesty</td><td>Lying, cheating or misrepresenting the truth for personal advantage</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Effects of Corruption on Individuals and Society</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Erosion of trust between citizens and leaders.</li><li>Misallocation of public resources away from development.</li><li>Increased poverty and inequality.</li><li>Weakening of institutions and the rule of law.</li><li>Loss of foreign investment and economic growth.</li><li>Moral decay and the normalisation of dishonesty.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Biblical Condemnation of Corruption</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Passage</th><th>Teaching</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Amos 5:12</td><td>God rebukes those who take bribes and deny justice to the needy</td></tr><tr><td>Micah 6:11</td><td>God condemns the use of dishonest scales and deceptive business weights</td></tr><tr><td>Proverbs 17:23</td><td>A wicked person accepts a bribe in secret to pervert the course of justice</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Christian Response to Corruption</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Living a life of honesty and integrity in private and public dealings.</li><li>Refusing to give or accept bribes.</li><li>Speaking out against corrupt practices.</li><li>Supporting and promoting transparency and accountability.</li><li>Praying for leaders and the nation to uphold justice.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span> <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Match each biblical reference (Amos 5:12, Micah 6:11, Proverbs 17:23) correctly to the form of corruption it condemns.</div>",
