    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Forgiveness</span> is the act of letting go of resentment, anger or the desire for revenge against someone who has wronged you, and is one of the central teachings of Christian living.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Forgiveness</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Forgiveness means choosing to release an offender from the guilt of their wrong against you, and no longer holding it against them, even though the wrong was real and may have caused genuine hurt.</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Biblical Teachings on Forgiveness</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Passage</th><th>Teaching</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Matthew 18:21–22</td><td>When Peter asks how often he should forgive, Jesus answers 'seventy times seven,' teaching that forgiveness should be limitless, not merely a fixed number of times</td></tr><tr><td>Luke 15:11–32</td><td>The Parable of the Prodigal Son shows a father who forgives and joyfully welcomes back his wayward son, illustrating God's readiness to forgive those who return to Him</td></tr><tr><td>Colossians 3:13</td><td>Believers are told to bear with one another and forgive, just as the Lord forgave them</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Importance of Forgiveness in Christian Living</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>It reflects the character and mercy of God toward us.</li><li>It is a condition for receiving God's own forgiveness (Matthew 6:14–15).</li><li>It restores broken relationships.</li><li>It demonstrates genuine Christian love in action.</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Benefits of Forgiveness to Individuals and Communities</h3><ul style=\"margin-left:20px;\"><li>Emotional and psychological healing; freedom from bitterness and stress.</li><li>Restoration of peace and harmony in relationships.</li><li>Reduced conflict and improved community cohesion.</li><li>Opportunity for reconciliation and renewed trust.</li><li>A positive Christian witness to others.</li></ul><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span> <strong>Summary:</strong> Forgiveness is not optional for the Christian; it is both commanded and modelled by God, and it benefits the one who forgives as much as the one forgiven.</div>",
